I believe the point in waiting is that if you wish for an intelligent
artifact at XL 1, the blast is likely to kill you.  So you need to
gain a few levels first.

I agree with you that the speed boots should've come earlier.  Then
again, if he'd needed to run away from anything (not bloody likely
with DSM at XL1/DL1) he could've always wished for them there and
then.  So it was a mistake, but hardly a serious one.

As for your suggestion of an "oLS, to me, in that situation, that's
something of a toss-up against the green dragon meat.  One will save
you from more kinds of instadeaths, and will continue to be valuable
even after you get intrinsic poison resistance (which should be soon
anyway).  The other will save you from only one common class of
instadeaths, but will do so as many times as needed rather than just
once, and, as a bonus, will feed you.

Either way, neither is particularly useful on its own: their purpose
is just to make sure that, after this really promising start, the
character won't go and die a YAreallySD.


